"LICENSE 3.1" / "LICENSE 3.2" — what the phrase in the sources means
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Twenty-seven comments in this tree explain a removal with "left with LICENSE
3.1" or "LICENSE 3.2".  They cite a numbered document that is not in this
distribution and never was: the LICENSE file beside this one is plain
Apache-2.0 and has no such sections.  Rather than rewrite the history those
comments record, the term is defined here, once, so the citations resolve:

    3.1  the EFIT lineage — libefit.so, the EFIT forward/inverse driver, the
         Green-table generator (efund) and its tables, and every recorded
         output of them.  Removed outright; the replacement is this project's
         own Grad-Shafranov solve in rust/fylite/src/{equilibrium,inverse}.rs.

    3.2  the GACODE-binding shared libraries — libneo.so, libgeo.so,
         libtglf.so — and the ctypes bindings written around them.  The CODE
         they bound is Apache-2.0 and its translations are attributed below;
         what left was the vendored binaries, not the right to derive.

Both removals kept the recorded answers (tests/data/FYDOC-CASE-03-frozen-libs/corpus/), because a fixture is
not the code that produced it.  ★If you are adding a comment, say what left
and why in your own words — a phrase whose referent has to be looked up in a
licence file is not an explanation.

