DERIVED WORK — EPEDNN.jl (Apache-2.0)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The H-mode pedestal surrogate is a TRANSCRIPTION of EPEDNN.jl's evaluation, and
the numbers it evaluates are that model's own weights.

    Upstream:  ProjectTorreyPines/EPEDNN.jl,
               https://github.com/ProjectTorreyPines/EPEDNN.jl
               model `delta_ne_sqrt_power` in `data/EPED1NNmodel.bson`
    Terms:     Apache License 2.0 (a copy travels at
               rust/tools/data/EPEDNN-LICENSE, beside the BSON it applies to)
    Authors:   O. Meneghini / General Atomics and the EPEDNN.jl contributors

Files in this distribution that derive from it:

    rust/fylite/src/pedestal.rs        <- EPEDNN.jl::pedestal_array, line for
                                          line: the ten inputs and their order,
                                          `delta += 1` and the absolute values,
                                          the per-output power law, the MLP
                                          correction with its scaling, plus
                                          ::extrapolation_distance and
                                          ::effective_triangularity
    rust/fylite/src/pedestal_tables.rs <- the model's numbers, extracted by
                                          rust/tools/extract_epednn.py from the
                                          vendored BSON (a 10->32->32->32->18
                                          GELU MLP and the power-law
                                          coefficients); the sha256 of the copy
                                          is stamped into the generated header
                                          and re-checked by the extractor

STATEMENT OF CHANGES.  Julia to Rust; the weights are generated into the source
rather than read from a BSON at runtime, so the shipped library has no model
file to lose.  The out-of-box behaviour is upstream's and deliberately so —
inputs outside the training box are answered WITH the extrapolation distance
reported rather than refused.  What this port adds is a refusal for a machine
that cannot be normalized at all (non-finite, or a non-positive
size / field / current / density), where upstream would evaluate anyway.

★The model is EPED1-NN (Meneghini et al., Nucl. Fusion 57 (2017) 086034), a
neural-network surrogate of EPED (Snyder et al., Phys. Plasmas 16 (2009)
056118).  The FULL EPED model is a stability-code scan (ELITE); nothing here
derives from it or from ELITE.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NOT INCLUDED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This distribution deliberately contains no machine description, no experimental
data, and no code or recorded output of the EFIT lineage.  See README.md
("What this distribution does not contain").

Nor does it contain the four Fortran shared libraries the ports were checked
against — libefit.so, libneo.so, libgeo.so, libtglf.so — or any binding to them.
What survives of them is a set of RECORDED answers under tests/data/FYDOC-CASE-03-frozen-libs/corpus/, captured
at the Python API boundary before they left; tests/data/INDEX.md says what is in
there and python/fylite/_oracle.py reads it.  A recorded answer is a fixture,
not a licence to redistribute the code that produced it.


--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAMED BUT NOT DERIVED
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Three more third-party projects are named in this tree.  None of them is a
source of code here, and saying so is the point — a reader who meets the name in
a comment should be able to find out immediately what the relationship is.

    TGLFNN.jl (Apache-2.0) and EPEDNN.jl
        `rust/fylite/src/nn.rs` implements one ARCHITECTURE FAMILY — a dense
        input layer, optional plain depth, optional residual blocks, a dense
        output layer — whose shape was read off the SHIPPED MODEL FILES of those
        two surrogates.  No code from either is translated into it and NO
        WEIGHTS are compiled into the library or the wasm: the numbers arrive as
        caller-supplied slices.  Both are ORACLES for it (registry record V-02:
        this evaluator against upstream's own evaluation).  EPEDNN.jl is a
        derived work HERE only through `pedestal.rs` / `pedestal_tables.rs`,
        which the section above attributes.

    ukaea/tglfnn-ukaea (LGPL)
        `rust/tools/export_tglfnn_ukaea.py` calls it and deliberately does not
        vendor it: upstream is copyleft (its LICENSE says 2.1, its
        pyproject.toml says 3.0) and this project is not.  The ruling
        (2026-08-30) is「call it, do not vendor it」— the weights stay in the
        user's own checkout, the export lands OUTSIDE this repository, and
        `$FYLITE_NN_DIR` points the host at it.  Nothing from that repository
        enters this distribution, and that script enforces it.

    google-deepmind/fusion_surrogates (software Apache-2.0, weights CC-BY-4.0)
        `rust/tools/export_qlknn_7_11.py` exports the QLKNN_7_11 network for the
        host to load.  The export is DATA under a different licence from the
        code that reads it, so the upstream LICENSE and NOTICE travel beside the
        exported file rather than being folded into this one; upstream asks that
        doi:10.1063/1.5134126 be cited when a number it produces is quoted.  The
        kernel itself is unchanged by that integration (registry record V-03).
